# Keep the local build out of the image build context.
#
# This matters more than it looks. Every Dockerfile here does `COPY . .` after restoring, so without
# this file the host's `bin/` and `obj/` land in the container and the in-container restore reuses
# them — with a project.assets.json written against the host's SDK and absolute host paths. The
# symptom is a restore or publish that fails for reasons that have nothing to do with the change
# being built, and only in CI or only locally depending on whose tree was dirtier.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.idea/
**/.git/
**/.gitignore
**/.dockerignore
**/*.user
**/node_modules/

# Nothing in the image needs these, and the WASM build context is the whole repo.
docs/
mockups/
*.docx
*.dump
.claude/
.nodeterm/
